# The constants an app must agree with the kernel on.
#
# An app is a separate ESP-IDF project and so is configured separately -- but it
# is loaded into the kernel's FreeRTOS and calls into it, so the two have to
# agree on everything the app hands across that boundary as a TickType_t.
#
# CONFIG_FREERTOS_HZ is the one that bit. pdMS_TO_TICKS() is a macro, expanded
# in the app's own build against the app's CONFIG_FREERTOS_HZ, but the tick it
# computes a count for is the kernel's -- so a mismatch makes every delay the
# app asks for wrong in a way that is invisible until it runs. At 100 against
# the kernel's 250, a nominal 20 ms becomes 8, and anything under 10 ms becomes
# zero ticks, which vTaskDelay() treats as a yield and not a sleep. Measured:
# Doom's mixer ran 256 idle iterations in 45 ms and produced audio at 169206
# frames a second where 44100 was wanted, which is heard as distortion.
#
# The kernel's value is in sdkconfig.defaults at the top of the tree, and
# tools/build-apps.sh refuses to stage an app whose value differs.
CONFIG_FREERTOS_HZ=250

# The socket count, for the same reason and one more. lwIP numbers its sockets
# from LWIP_SOCKET_OFFSET, which is FD_SETSIZE minus this -- the kernel's own
# select() and poll() use *its* value when they translate a descriptor. An app's
# headers also let lwIP define FD_SETSIZE from this number, but only when lwIP's
# sockets.h wins the include race against newlib's FD_SET; when it does, an app
# built with IDF's default of 10 passes a two-word fd_set to a kernel filling in
# one sized for 40. Either way the two builds have to say the same number.
CONFIG_LWIP_MAX_SOCKETS=40
